WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.360
A man is convicted of murder.

2
00:00:02.410 --> 00:00:04.540
The court has heard the evidence.

3
00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:09.740
In classical Islamic law, what happens
next is not up to the judge alone.

4
00:00:09.790 --> 00:00:12.130
The victim's family has a choice.

5
00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:13.210
Retribution.

6
00:00:13.260 --> 00:00:14.670
Compensation.

7
00:00:14.720 --> 00:00:16.400
Or forgiveness.

8
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:19.990
Why would the law hand a
grieving family that power?

9
00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:23.690
In this mission, you'll sort
punishments into three kinds:

10
00:00:23.740 --> 00:00:27.610
fixed, retribution, and
the judge's discretion.

11
00:00:27.660 --> 00:00:30.780
Then you'll read two verses
on the law of equality,

12
00:00:30.830 --> 00:00:33.940
and ask how retribution could save life.

13
00:00:33.990 --> 00:00:38.690
Your mission: find out why Islamic
law gives the family that power.
